I reviewed `XmlGenUtils` and replaced a repetitive conditional chain with a data table.

## What I changed (`jadx-core/.../jadx/core/xmlgen/XmlGenUtils.java`)

`getAttrTypeAsString` was eight near-identical blocks:
```java
String s = "";
if ((type & ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_REFERENCE) != 0) { s += "|reference"; }
if ((type & ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_STRING)    != 0) { s += "|string"; }
// ...6 more...
if (s.isEmpty()) { return null; }
return s.substring(1);
```

Now the flag→name correspondence is a single ordered table, and one loop does the work:
```java
private static final Map<Integer, String> ATTR_TYPE_NAMES = new LinkedHashMap<>();
static {
    ATTR_TYPE_NAMES.put(ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_REFERENCE, "reference");
    // ...in the same order as before...
    ATTR_TYPE_NAMES.put(ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_FRACTION, "fraction");
}

public static String getAttrTypeAsString(int type) {
    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
    ATTR_TYPE_NAMES.forEach((flag, name) -> {
        if ((type & flag) != 0) {
            sb.append('|').append(name);
        }
    });
    if (sb.length() == 0) {
        return null;
    }
    return sb.substring(1);
}
```

This removes the eight-fold duplication, makes the flag set a single source of truth, and drops the repeated `String +=` in favor of one `StringBuilder`.

## Why it's safe
- **Order preserved:** `LinkedHashMap` iterates in insertion order, which matches the original if-chain order, so the emitted `|a|b|...` string is byte-identical.
- **Keys are safe:** the `ATTR_TYPE_*` constants are `protected static final int` in `ParserConstants` with distinct values (`1`…`1<<7`), so there are no `Integer`-key collisions; empty result still returns `null`, and `substring(1)` still strips the leading `|`.
- **Access unchanged:** I kept the exact `ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_*` reference path the original used; `XmlGenUtils` is in the same package as `ParserConstants`, so the `protected` access is valid.
- Added `LinkedHashMap`/`Map` imports; `HashSet`/`Set` are still used by `makeXmlDump`. Braces balanced (20/20). Verified by inspection (module not buildable here without network/cached deps).

Working tree now has uncommitted changes across eight files (`Utils`, `StringUtils`, `TypeUtils`, `AccessInfo`, `RegionUtils`, `AnnotationGen`, `NameMapper`, `XmlGenUtils`). Still not committed — happy to commit on your say-so.

