The class wrote comma-separated lists to the `ICodeWriter` in three places — annotation values (`formatAnnotation`), `addThrows`, and the `ENCODED_ARRAY` case in `encodeValue` — each repeating the same iterator + `if (it.hasNext()) code.add(", ")` separator dance (the file even carried a `// TODO: refactor this boilerplate code`). I extracted one small helper:

```java
private <T> void addSeparated(ICodeWriter code, Iterable<T> items, Consumer<T> appender) {
    for (Iterator<T> it = items.iterator(); it.hasNext();) {
        appender.accept(it.next());
        if (it.hasNext()) {
            code.add(", ");
        }
    }
