I reviewed `XmlGenUtils` and replaced a repetitive conditional chain with a data table.

## What I changed (`jadx-core/.../jadx/core/xmlgen/XmlGenUtils.java`)

`getAttrTypeAsString` was eight near-identical blocks:
```java
String s = "";
if ((type & ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_REFERENCE) != 0) { s += "|reference"; }
if ((type & ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_STRING)    != 0) { s += "|string"; }
// ...6 more...
if (s.isEmpty()) { return null; }
return s.substring(1);
```

Now the flag→name correspondence is a single ordered table, and one loop does the work:
```java
private static final Map<Integer, String> ATTR_TYPE_NAMES = new LinkedHashMap<>();
static {
    ATTR_TYPE_NAMES.put(ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_REFERENCE, "reference");
    // ...in the same order as before...
    ATTR_TYPE_NAMES.put(ValuesParser.ATTR_TYPE_FRACTION, "fraction");
}

public static String getAttrTypeAsString(int type) {
    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
    ATTR_TYPE_NAMES.forEach((flag, name) -> {
        if ((type & flag) != 0) {
            sb.append('|').append(name);
        }
    });
    if (sb.length() == 0) {
        return null;
    }
    return sb.substring(1);
}
```

This removes the eight-fold duplication, makes the flag set a single source of truth, and drops the repeated `String +=` in favor of one `StringBuilder`.

